And he looks at me and he goes, "Nick,

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:08.200
these are Ivy League kids."

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:16.040
Like these kids are Ivy League students

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:17.640
at Cornell. They're on the sports teams.

00:01:16.040 --> 00:01:19.200
And we are sitting here complaining

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:20.040
about them.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:21.800
Hm.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:23.520
Maybe it's us.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:25.080
Maybe it's us.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:27.200
And we're like, "Holy shit." And we both

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:28.920
kind of soak in. We order another beer.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.440
And we're like,

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:33.280
"It is us."

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:35.280
Yeah. It's our fault. It's our fault.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:37.600
So, what we did was we simplified the

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:39.240
job.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.600
We had We had employees out there who

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:42.080
were doing

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:44.240
10 jobs

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:45.480
or 15 jobs. We actually had a a tablet

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:47.880
that they worked with. And on the back

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:49.800
of the tablet, we we we posted a piece

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:50.960
of paper with all the things they needed

00:01:49.800 --> 00:01:53.280
to remember to do for a pickup. And it

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:54.400
was like 28 items long. Hm.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:55.960
They got to make the schedules. They got

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.720
to call the customers. They got to

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:59.120
create the invoice. Size all the boxes.

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.360
They were actually creating each of

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:01.840
these hourly employees who work

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:04.360
seasonally for us were creating every

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:05.440
invoice and measuring boxes. Like just

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:07.240
looking at a box and saying, "Oh, that's

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:08.840
a medium box or a large box." That's $10

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:10.039
difference in revenue, by the way. A

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:10.840
medium box or a large box. They're

00:02:10.039 --> 00:02:12.320
standing there right in front of the

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:13.200
customer who's like looking over their

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.200
shoulder while they're making the

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:16.040
invoice.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.120
Um just on and on and on. They were

00:02:16.040 --> 00:02:18.240
doing the whole pickup. They were

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.120
organizing things. They were labeling

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:21.560
things. They were going back to the

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:23.560
warehouse, unloading the entire truck.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:24.880
So, we had temp employees who had 29

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:25.720
things to do.

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:27.000
Yeah.

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:29.240
We figured out a way to get it down to

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:30.640
five key things. Somebody else is going

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:32.000
to make the schedules.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:34.280
Somebody else is going to ask customer

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:35.520
service somebody in the Philippines is

00:02:34.280 --> 00:02:36.720
going to answer customer service calls.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:38.080
If If you get a question you don't have

00:02:36.720 --> 00:02:38.880
to answer, hand them a card. They're

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:39.680
going to call this number and they're

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.480
going to talk to somebody who knows

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:43.200
what's going on. Your job is a driver.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:45.680
You don't answer questions. Don't tell

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.720
them you don't know. Don't make [ __ ] up.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:48.560
Then when it comes to the invoice, take

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:49.800
a picture of the invoice, upload it to

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:51.280
the iPad,

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.800
and then somebody sitting at a computer

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:54.080
full-time who's really good at making

00:02:52.800 --> 00:02:56.040
invoices is going to make every single

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:57.640
invoice for our whole company.

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:58.800
So, we went line by line by line by line

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:00.280
by line

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:04.120
and we said, "Okay.

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:04.120
Drive the truck and don't hit anything.

00:03:04.239 --> 00:03:06.800
Let the customers know when you're

00:03:05.519 --> 00:03:09.000
coming.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:11.080
Make sure every box is labeled.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:13.320
Take the pictures and put it all in the

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:14.600
truck in the right way.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:15.800
Then somebody else is going to come pick

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:16.519
that full truck up from you, take it

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:17.400
back to the warehouse. A totally

00:03:16.519 --> 00:03:20.080
different team's going to unload it at

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:21.800
the warehouse. When we did that, guys,

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:23.239
our revenue doubled and our stress

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.920
shrunk in half.

00:03:23.239 --> 00:03:29.040
Mhm. So, we made we made three times as

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:29.040
